class:: GendyField
summary:: Independent stochastic sound and silence fields
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>GENDY
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Guides/Stochastica-GENDY, Classes/Gendy77, Classes/Gendy91, Classes/GendyS709, Classes/GendyPerc, Classes/GendyInterp, Classes/GendyDiffusion, Classes/GendyCoupled

description::
strong::Historically informed PARAG subset.::

Outputs one control-rate gate per voice. At each field boundary, a local stream draws an exponential duration and a Bernoulli activity choice. This separates waveform microstructure from macro-level activity, following the PARAG timing account in Luque (2006), printed p. 29, and Hoffmann (2000), p. 34: link::https://sergioluque.com/stochastics:: and link::https://rohandrape.net/ut/rttcc-text/Hoffmann2000a.pdf::.

This is not a reconstruction of PARAG's complete sections, voice settings or historical output. Field boundaries need not change a gate: consecutive active fields join, as do consecutive silent fields. Each voice has its own derived PCG seed, so increasing voice count preserves existing voice streams. Changing duration/probability affects the next field. Reset restarts all voice clocks and RNGs together.

At most eight field boundaries are processed per control calculation, retaining negative time remainder if overloaded. Mean duration has a one-control-interval floor; individual exponential draws may be shorter. At dense settings the bounded scheduler can lag. Non-finite meanDuration uses one second and non-finite soundProb uses 0.5. Gates have sharp edges and do not fade audio; use Lag or an external envelope.

Like vanilla link::Classes/LFPulse::, each output alternates between zero and one. Here durations and activity are stochastic, and a new field may keep the same gate; there is no periodic duty cycle.

image::gendy-gendyfield.png::


classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: numVoices
Construction-time output count, clipped to 1..32. Each output has a separately derived local random stream.
argument:: meanDuration
Mean duration of a field in seconds, floored at one control interval and capped at 1e9. Sampled when a new field begins. Field durations are exponential; adjacent fields may share a gate, so this is not mean audible gate dwell.
argument:: soundProb
Bernoulli activity probability 0..1, sampled at each new field. Zero chooses silence, one chooses sound. Changing it does not interrupt the current field.
argument:: reset
Nonpositive-to-positive edge rewinds all voice streams and field clocks. The reset sample equals the first sample of a fresh instance; a held positive value does not keep resetting. Audio-rate reset is supported.
argument:: seed
Construction-time local PCG32 seed. Nonzero seeds repeat for identical inputs and rate. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth RNG once; reset reuses it. Cross-platform last-bit differences are possible.
returns::
An array of numVoices control-rate gates, or one signal when numVoices is one.

examples::
subsection:: Minimal example
code::
(
{
    var gate = GendyField.kr(1, 0.35, 0.7, seed: 91);
    SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.07) ! 2 * Lag.kr(gate, 0.02) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::

subsection:: Six independent activity fields
Pitch behavior lives in each waveform voice; independent field clocks organize entrances and rests. Fades suppress gate clicks.
code::
(
{
    var gates = GendyField.kr(6, 0.4, 0.55, seed: 99);
    var voices = Array.fill(6, { |i|
        var f = 80 * (1.25 ** i);
        LeakDC.ar(Gendy91.ar(minFreq: f, maxFreq: f * 1.4,
            durPrimaryRatio: 0.01, seed: 100 + i)) * Lag.kr(gates[i], 0.025) * 0.035
    });
    Splay.ar(voices) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
